 **Data Structures:**
-The data is stored as a hierarchy of coefficients. For a 3D volume, the DWT decomposes the data into subbands. At each level $l$, the data is split into approximation coefficients $A_l$ (low-pass in all dimensions) and detail coefficients $D_l^{xyz}$ (high-pass in one or more dimensions). Specifically, there are 7 detail subbands per level: $f_{HHH}, f_{HHL}, f_{HLH}, f_{HLL}, f_{LHH}, f_{LHL}, f_{LLH}$ [S3][S5, unofficial]. The structure is typically organized in an octree or brick-based hierarchy where each node contains the coefficients for a specific spatial block at a specific resolution level [S3].
